NAME
       sync - write cached data to the disk

SYNOPSIS
       sync

DESCRIPTION
       The ext2 file system keeps modified blocks in memory and writes them to
       the disk a little later (after a few seconds, or when the cache fills
       up). **sync** forces all of these dirty blocks onto the disk at once and
       returns when the write is done.

       Run it before switching off a machine that is not shut down with
       **poweroff**(8) or **reboot**(8), and before taking a disk away. A
       FAT32 boot partition mounted on /boot is written through at once and
       needs no sync.

EXIT STATUS
       0 on success, 1 if the data could not be written.

SEE ALSO
       poweroff(1), reboot(1)
